ing, Information Systems, and/or equivalent formal training or work experience\n* Two (2\\) – four (4\\) years related experience (analysis, programing, design, debugging, testing, etc.)\n* Demonstrated experience in programming languages such as C\\#, Python\n* Experience with reporting tools such as SSRS, Power BI\n* Experience with ETL tools like SSIS or Azure Data Factory\n* Familiarity with GitHub Copilot or other AI coding assistant\n* Strong SQL skills, Git Source Control\n* Experience with Visual Studio, VS code and Azure DevOps\n* Financial Industry experience preferred\n* Computer hardware, operating system (Windows) and software/application (MS Office, Outlook etc.) skills\n* Strong problem solving and decision\\-making skills\n* Self\\-development skills to keep up to date with fast\\-changing trends\n\n\n \\*Must be eligible to work in the U.S. without sponsorship now or in the future.\\*\n   \n\n  \n\n*The above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by individuals in, or assigned to, the above position and are not intended to be construed as an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties and skills required, and may be changed at the discretion of the Company.*\n**About Us**\n Founded in 1998 and headquartered in Dallas, Texas, Hilltop Holdings offers a diverse range of financial services through its three primary subsidiaries, PlainsCapital Bank, PrimeLending, and HilltopSecurities. PlainsCapital Bank is a leading commercial bank with locations throughout Texas. PrimeLending is a national mortgage provider focused on purchase mortgage originations. HilltopSecurities provides financial advisory, clearing, retail brokerage, and other investment banking services. Hilltop Holdings seeks to build the premier Texas\\-based diversified financial services holding company through acquisitions and organic growth. To learn more, please visit www.hilltop.com .\n   \n\n  \n\n**About The Team**\n The Information Technology department at Hilltop Holdings is a forward\\-thinking team dedicated to delivering innovative technological solutions that drive success in the financial services industry. Our department leverages cutting\\-edge technologies to enhance operational efficiency, customer experiences, and ensure the security and integrity of our systems and data. We are committed to staying at the forefront of technological advancements, constantly exploring new opportunities in emerging trends. Our team fosters a collaborative and respectful work environment. We empower our talented professionals to develop creative solutions and drive digital transformation across the organization. With a strong focus on agility and adaptability, our department is instrumental in enabling Hilltop to stay ahead of the curve in an ever\\-evolving digital landscape.","https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4428068404":"We are a growing medical technology company is seeking a Senior Software Test Engineer to lead the design, development, and execution of testing strategies for complex medical device systems. This role combines hands\\-on system\\-level testing with ownership of automated testing frameworks to ensure product quality, reliability, and regulatory compliance.\n \n\n\n\n The ideal candidate will have experience driving verification and validation activities while developing scalable automation solutions in a highly collaborative engineering environment.\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Responsibilities** \n\n\n\n* Design and execute comprehensive test strategies, test plans, and test cases for medical device systems.\n* Perform functional, integration, system\\-level, and performance testing.\n* Lead verification and validation (V\\&V) activities in accordance with applicable regulatory requirements.\n* Investigate defects, conduct root cause analysis, and partner with engineering teams to resolve issues.\n* Review product requirements and system architecture to ensure adequate test coverage and testability.\n* Generate validation documentation, test reports, and traceability artifacts.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Test Automation \\& Framework Development** \n\n\n\n* Design, develop, and maintain automated test frameworks and infrastructure.\n* Create automated test scripts using Python, C/C\\+\\+, or similar programming languages.\n* Integrate automated testing into CI/CD pipelines to support continuous validation.\n* Improve testing efficiency, reliability, and coverage through automation initiatives.\n* Evaluate and implement new testing tools and technologies.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Cross\\-Functional Collaboration** \n\n\n\n* Partner with software, hardware, systems, and quality teams to establish testing strategies and quality objectives.\n* Support system integration, product bring\\-up, and troubleshooting activities.\n* Collaborate with manufacturing and field teams on failure analysis and issue resolution.\n* Mentor junior engineers and contribute technical leadership to testing best practices.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Qualifications** \n\n\n\n* Bachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Biomedical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a related technical discipline.\n* 5\\+ years of experience in software testing, system validation, quality engineering, or medical device development.\n* Strong understanding of system\\-level testing across software, hardware, and integrated systems.\n* Experience developing and maintaining automated test frameworks.\n* Proficiency with Python, C/C\\+\\+, or similar programming languages.\n* Knowledge of verification and validation methodologies and defect tracking systems.\n* Hands\\-on experience with lab equipment, debugging, and troubleshooting complex systems.\n* Excellent analytical, problem\\-solving, and communication skills.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Preferred** \n\n\n\n* Experience in the medical device, healthcare technology, or other regulated industries.\n* Familiarity with Agile/Scrum development methodologies.\n* Experience with CI/CD environments and automated testing pipelines.\n* Working knowledge of Linux/Unix environments.\n* Background in both hardware and software testing.\n* Prior experience mentoring engineers or leading technical initiatives.\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Compensation** \n\n\n\n\n The anticipated salary range for this position is\n **$100,000–$130,000** \n plus bonuses. Final compensation will be determined based on experience, skills, education, and overall qualifications.","https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4428077753":"**This is a job that Jill, our AI Recruiter, is recruiting for on behalf of one of our customers.**\n She will pick the best candidates from Jack's network.\n   \n\n  \n\n The next step is to speak to Jack.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Job Title**\n Software Engineer, Platform\n   \n\n  \n\n**Salary**\n $200k\\-$250k \\+ Equity\n   \n\n  \n\n**Company Description**\n Duckbill is a $7\\.75M seed\\-funded San Francisco company backed by Heavybit and Uncork Capital, building Skyway to automate cloud cost management. Founded by domain experts with seven years of research, Duckbill provides the financial infrastructure used by AI labs and neoclouds to manage nine\\-figure infrastructure agreements.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Job Description**\n Join a high\\-impact team building Skyway, a financial platform for AI\\-native companies managing massive infrastructure costs. You will architect data systems processing hundreds of millions of billing rows using Python and ClickHouse. As one of the first ten engineers, you will own the infrastructure transforming unstructured cloud agreements into precise, actionable financial data.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Location**\n San Francisco, USA\n   \n\n  \n\n**Why this role is remarkable**\n* Direct impact on $10M\\+ compute decisions for the world's leading AI labs and neoclouds through your data models and financial engines.\n* Backed by $7\\.75M from Heavybit and Uncork Capital with a massi