inux systems and services in production\n  \n* 2\\+ years of experience developing reliable production\\-grade software in Java, Go, or other similar languages\n  \n* Proficiency with at least one automation technology such as Terraform, Chef, or Puppet\n  \n* Successfully designed and deployed mission\\-critical complex distributed systems\n  \n* Excellent critical thinking and communications skills with a desire to both learn from and educate your peers\n  \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n**Once you join, Wealthfront will:** \n  \n* Pair you with a 1:1 mentor to guide you through our onboarding program.\n  \n* Encourage you to lead impactful projects which match your professional goals.\n  \n* Support your professional development by providing feedback during weekly 1:1s and during our bi\\-annual reviews.\n  \n* Be given the opportunity to participate in designing systems and planning for the future of our infrastructure\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n Estimated annual salary range: $150,000 \\- $189,000 plus equity and a discretionary bonus.\n \n\n\n  \n\n\n  \n \n\n\n  \n\n\n Benefits include medical, vision, dental, 401K plan, generous time off, parental leave, wellness reimbursements, professional development, employee investing discount, and more!\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**About Wealthfront** \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n Here at Wealthfront, our mission is to create a financial system that favors people, not institutions. We do this by leveraging technology to build powerful, low\\-cost, and easy\\-to\\-use financial products that help modern investors grow and manage their money.\n \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n We started with the ambition to transform the investment advisory business. By automating strategies typically reserved for the wealthy, we unlocked access to high quality investment advice for a digitally\\-native generation that was underserved by traditional institutions. Since then, we've expanded to a full suite of products designed to help our clients turn their savings into long\\-term wealth, including:\n \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n • A Cash Account that, through our partner banks, offers one of the highest annual percentage yields on uninvested cash in the industry, while providing instant and secure access to your money with no account fees and a full suite of checking features.\n \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n • A zero\\-commission Stock Investing Account with 50\\+ handpicked collections that help DIY investors discover new companies and make smarter investing decisions.\n \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n • Multiple automated investing portfolios designed to unlock tax savings through sophisticated strategies like fixed income, tax\\-loss harvesting, and direct indexing—which we offer at industry\\-leading low costs and accessible minimums.\n \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n Our award\\-winning products have attracted over 1 million clients who trust us with more than $90 billion of their hard earned savings—and we're far from done. If you’re inspired to help us reshape the financial industry as we create our next chapter, let’s talk!\n \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n For more information please visit\n \n www.wealthfront.com\n \n .We are an equal opportunity employer and value diversity at our company. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status.\n \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Please review our** \n candidate privacy notice\n \n . \n \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n**Disclosures:** \n\n  All investing involves risk, including the possible loss of principal. Tax\\-Loss Harvesting benefits vary depending on the client's entire tax and investment profile. Wealthfront doesn’t provide tax advice. The Cash Account is offered by Wealthfront Brokerage LLC (“Wealthfront Brokerage”), Member of FINRA/SIPC. Wealthfront Brokerage is not a bank. We convey funds to partner banks who accept and maintain deposits, provide the variable interest rate, and provide access to FDIC pass\\-through insurance. Investment management and advisory services–which are not FDIC insured–are provided by Wealthfront Advisers LLC (“Wealthfront Advisers”), an SEC\\-registered investment adviser. The checking features offered in the Wealthfront Cash Account are provided by Green Dot Bank, Member FDIC. Fees and Eligibility requirements may apply to certain checking features, please see the\n \n Deposit Account Agreement\n \n for details.\n \n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n By “award\\-winning products”, please refer to\n \n www.wealthfront.com/reviews\n \n for more information. Wealthfront Corporation oversees Total Client Assets and Trusted Clients through Wealthfront Advisers and Wealthfront Brokerage. Wealthfront Advisers and Wealthfront Brokerage are wholly owned subsidiaries of Wealthfront Corporation.","https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4428097467":"**About The Company**\n TryApplyNow is a dynamic and innovative organization dedicated to transforming the recruitment landscape through cutting\\-edge technology and exceptional service. Our company specializes in providing comprehensive talent acquisition solutions tailored to meet the evolving needs of businesses across various industries. Committed to fostering a collaborative and inclusive work environment, TryApplyNow prides itself on its ability to attract top talent and deliver impactful results for our clients. We are passionate about leveraging data\\-driven insights and innovative tools to streamline hiring processes, enhance candidate experience, and drive organizational success.\n   \n\n  \n\n**About The Role**\n We are seeking a highly motivated and detail\\-oriented Recruitment Specialist to join our team. In this role, you will be responsible for managing the end\\-to\\-end recruitment process, from sourcing candidates to onboarding new hires. The ideal candidate will possess excellent communication skills, a strong understanding of various sourcing techniques, and the ability to build lasting relationships with candidates and hiring managers alike. This position offers an exciting opportunity to work in a fast\\-paced environment where your efforts directly contribute to the growth and success of our clients and organization. You will collaborate with cross\\-functional teams to identify talent needs, develop effective recruitment strategies, and ensure a seamless hiring experience.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Qualifications**\n The ideal candidate should possess a bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, or a related field. Proven experience in recruiting, talent acquisition, or a similar role is preferred. Strong understanding of sourcing tools, applicant tracking systems, and social media platforms is essential. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills are required to effectively engage with candidates and stakeholders. The ability to work independently, prioritize tasks, and adapt to changing priorities is crucial. Familiarity with employment laws and best practices in recruitment will be considered an advantage. A proactive approach, problem\\-solving skills, and a passion for connecting talent with opportunities are key attributes for success in this role.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Responsibilities**\n Develop and implement effective sourcing strategies to attract a diverse pool of qualified candidates. Manage the full recruitment cycle, including posting job openings, screening resumes, conducting interviews, and coordinating assessments. Build and maintain relationships with potential candidates through various channels, including social media, job boards, and networking events. Collaborate closely with hiring managers to understand their staffing needs and provide guidance on candidate selection. Maintain accurate and up\\-to\\-date records of recruitment activities within applicant tracking systems. Ensure a positive candidate experience by providing timely feedback and maintaining clear communication throughout the hiring process. Assist in employer branding initiatives to promote TryApplyNow as an employer of choice. Stay informed about industry trends and best practices to continuously improve recruitment strategies and processes.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Benefits**\n At TryApplyNow, we believe in rewarding our team members with competitive benefits that support their professional and personal growth. We offer comprehensive health insurance plans, including medical, dental, and vision coverage. Employees enjoy paid time off, including vacation, sick leave, and holidays. We provide opportunities for ongoing training and development to enhance your skills and career progression. Our organization fosters a flexible work environment, encouraging work\\-life balance. Additionally, employees have access to performance\\-based incentives and recognition programs. We are committed to creating an inclusive workplace where diversity is celebrated, and every team member feels valued and empowered to contribute to our collective success.\n   \n\n  \n\n Equal Opportunity\n   \n\n  \n\n TryApplyNow is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to fostering an inclusive environment where all employees and applicants are treated fairly and with respect. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, or any other protected characteristic. Our hiring decisions are based solely on qualifications, skills, and merit. We believe that diverse perspectives and backgrounds strengthen our organization and enable us to better serve our clients and communities. We encourage individuals from all backgrounds to apply and join our team in shaping the future of talent acquisition.","https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4428096502":"**This is a remote position.**\n Ad Hoc is a technology company that empowers organizations to deliver scalable, impactful digital services. Using modern, agile methods, our team creates products that meet people’s needs and transform their experience of government.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Work on things that matter**\n Our collaborations have shaped some of the defining moments in public\\-sector service delivery. We’ve helped build products that connect Veterans to tailored services, help millions access affordable health care, and support important programs like Head Start. As we work with agencies to deliver critical services, we’re also changing how the government approaches technology.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Built for a remote life**\n Our culture, communications, and tools are built for remote work, enabling us to bring together top talent nationwide. At Ad Hoc, remote life empowers our teams to design work environments that fit their lives and that foster flexibility and collaboration to achieve positive outcomes for our customers.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Committed to high expectations and a welcoming culture**\n Ad Hoc values acceptance, accountability, and humility. We aren’t heroes. We learn from our mistakes and improve the process for the next time. We build small, inclusive teams to collaborate closely with our partners to solve the right problems and deliver software that works.\n   \n\n  \n\n The\n **Federal Civilian** \n business unit supports many customers spanning the federal, commercial, and nonprofit space. Our customers include NASA, the General Services Administration, Office of Personnel Management, the Library of Congress, Health \\& Human Services, and the FDIC. We partner with these agencies to build new capabilities, deliver products, establish data as a strategic asset for informed decision\\-making, modernize legacy systems, and build the digital service infrastructure necessary to scale their mission impact.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Primary Responsibilities**\n Software Engineer II \\- Front End/ Back End serves as an individual contributor within a team; with the support and guidance of leadership, you will be responsible for supporting the goal of meeting scope, schedule and delivery requirements. You will begin to develop an awareness and understanding of the engineering function within the program, as well as interact with stakeholders. Primary expectations for a Software Engineer II \\- Front End/ Back End include:\n   \n\n  \n\n* Estimates and completes development tasks including coding, requirements gathering, and analysis with a moderate level of feedback and guidance from their team\n* Debugs, optimizes, maintains, and monitors their work in both test and production environments\n* Develops tests, monitoring/instrumentation, analytics, and deployment pipeline changes as appropriate for the given task\n* Participates in on\\-call rotations with their team as necessary\n* Builds technical and communication skills, gaining context around surrounding areas\n* Participates in planning sessions, building an understanding of major architectures and design patterns\n* Actively participates in design and asks questions to work toward understanding of technical trade\\-offs, interactions, and dependencies in the system\n* Development of influential skills to help make tactical decisions and support onboarding for new developers\n* Exhibits understanding for other roles and practices, including how they are intended to work together\n\n\n**Required Qualifications \\& Experience**\n* Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or related field and 5\\+ years of experience\n* Golang\n* Angular\n* Cloud Experience (ideally AWS)\n* SQL experience\n* Knowledge of software development methodologies, tools, and processes.\n* Excellent problem\\-solving and analytical skills.\n* Ability to write clear, concise code using commenting when appropriate\n* Good understanding of CI/CD pipelines backed by Jenkins.\n\n\n**Nice\\-to\\-have Qualifications \\& Experience**\n* Health Care Industry and/or CMS experience\n* Experience on multiple Scrum teams in a variety of different contexts (different team sizes, different organizations, different cultures, co\\-located vs. distributed, etc.)\n* Excellent oral and written communication skills, with an ability to communicate complex technical topics to management and non\\-technical audiences\n* Prior experience in a client\\-facing consulting or contracting role\n* Works well as a team member in a fast\\-paced and often time\\-sensitive environment\n* Prior professional services, government, or federal consulting experience\n* Experience building digital healthcare technology products and services\n* Experience working in the public sector or a highly regulated industry\n* Familiarity with (508\\) accessibility requirements\n\n\n**Security Clearance Requirements**\n* US Citizenship\n* US Residency for at least the past 3 years\n* Able to meet the requirements to hold a position of Public Trust, including successful completion of a US Government background investigation\n* Disclaimer: Medical or recreational marijuana use is considered illegal at the federal level, regardless of state laws allowing such, and may affect your ability to obtain Public Trust. See article\n\n\n**To learn more about working at Ad Hoc, please visit:** \n https://adhocteam.us/join\n   \n\n  \n\n**Benefits**\n* Company\\-subsidized health, dental, and vision insurance\n* Flexible PTO\n* 401K with employer match\n* Paid parental leave after one year of service\n* Employee Assistance Program\n\n\n Ad Hoc LLC is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, age, pregnancy, disability, work\\-related injury, covered veteran status, political ideology, marital status, or any other factor that the law protects from employment discrimination.\n   \n\n  \n\n We value the unique skills gained through military service and encourage veterans and transitioning service members to apply.\n   \n\n  \n\n In support of various state and city equal pay transparency laws, Ad Hoc job descriptions feature the starting range we reasonably expect to pay to candidates who would join our team with little to no need for training on the responsibilities we've outlined above. Actual compensation is influenced by a wide range of factors including but not limited to skill set, level of experience, and responsibility. The range of starting pay for this role is $xxx\\-$xxx. Our recruiters will be happy to answer any questions you may have, and we look forward to learning more about your salary requirements.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Job Reference**\n https://adhoc.team/","https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4428091527":"**At Cadence, we hire and develop leaders and innovators who want to make an impact on the world of technology.**\n**About The Role**\n Cadence Design Systems is looking for a highly motivated Software Engineer II to join the Innovus R\\&D team. Innovus is Cadence’s flagship digital implementation platform, enabling customers to design advanced semiconductor chips from RTL to GDSII.\n   \n\n  \n\n In this role, you will contribute to the development of next\\-generation physical design technologies, including placement, routing, and optimization. You will work on high\\-performance, scalable systems that power advanced semiconductor design flows.\n   \n\n  \n\n Key Responsibilities\n   \n\n  \n\n* Design, implement, and optimize algorithms for physical synthesis, placement, and routing engines\n* Develop high\\-performance, scalable software using C/C\\+\\+ on Linux/UNIX platforms\n* Contribute to the Innovus digital implementation flow, including timing, power, and optimization\n* Collaborate with cross\\-functional teams to define requirements and deliver high\\-quality solutions\n* Analyze performance bottlenecks and improve runtime, scalability, and quality of results (PPA)\n* Debug, troubleshoot, and enhance existing features within the Innovus platform\n\n\n**Minimum Qualifications**\n* MS in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, or related field\n* Strong foundation in algorithms, data structures, and problem\\-solving\n* Proficiency in C/C\\+\\+ and software development on UNIX/Linux systems\n* Strong analytical and debugging skills\n* Ability to work effectively in a collaborative, team\\-oriented environment\n\n\n*The annual salary range for California is $101,500 to $188,500\\. You may also be eligible to receive incentive compensation: bonus, equity, and benefits. Sales positions generally offer a competitive On Target Earnings (OTE) incentive compensation structure. Please note that the salary range is a guideline and compensation may vary based on factors such as qualifications, skill level, competencies and work location. Our benefits programs include: paid vacation and paid holidays, 401(k) plan with employer match, employee stock purchase plan, a variety of medical, dental and vision plan options, and more.*\n**We’re doing work that matters. Help us solve what others can’t.**","https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4428090851":"**About The Company**\n At Boeing, we are dedicated to pushing the boundaries of innovation and collaboration to create a better world. As a leading aerospace company, Boeing designs, manufactures, and supports commercial airplanes, defense, space, and security systems. Our commitment to excellence, integrity, and sustainability drives us to develop cutting\\-edge solutions that serve our customers and communities worldwide. We foster a culture of diversity, inclusion, and continuous learning, providing our employees with opportunities for professional growth and impactful work. Join us to be part of a global team that makes a difference in the world.\n   \n\n  \n\n**About The Role**\n The Boeing Company is seeking a highly skilled Systems Software Engineer (Associate, Experienced, or Senior) to join our Software Development team within the Phantom Works Network Centric Operations group located in Berkeley, Missouri. This role primarily supports Boeing Defense, Space \\& Security (BDS) Software Engineering organization. As a key contributor, you will be involved in designing, developing, and implementing platform\\-agnostic software capabilities that enable network operations for tactical fighter aircraft. The position requires a collaborative mindset, commitment to customer satisfaction, and a passion for solving complex problems through ingenuity and innovation.\n   \n\n  \n\n In this role, you will work closely with software architects, data analysts, and customer teams to derive and implement data fusion algorithms, analyze sensor data, and develop prototypes using languages such as C\\+\\+, Python, and MATLAB. You will also be responsible for documenting technical requirements, analyzing the effectiveness of data fusion techniques, and supporting process improvements across multiple contracts and programs. The position offers an exciting opportunity to contribute to advanced aerospace systems that impact national security and defense capabilities.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Qualifications**\n Qualified candidates will possess a Bachelor's Degree in engineering, computer science, data science, physics, or a related field, along with relevant industry experience. The ideal candidate will have at least 2 years of experience working with data fusion engines, kinematic correlation techniques, Kalman filters, and sensor data fusion technologies. Experience with pattern recognition, multi\\-modal sensor data, sensor calibration, and visualization tools is highly desirable.\n   \n\n  \n\n Additional requirements include familiarity with sensors such as Radar and infrared sensors, proficiency in probabilistic models like Bayesian reasoning and Kalman filtering, and a strong foundation in advanced probability statistics. Candidates should demonstrate a self\\-starter attitude, high ethical standards, analytical and creative problem\\-solving skills, and the ability to work effectively under pressure in a dynamic environment.\n   \n\n  \n\n Preferred qualifications involve extensive experience in software development related to data fusion analysis, a proven track record of working with sensor management systems, and experience developing algorithms for complex aerospace applications. Candidates with a higher level of experience (up to 17\\+ years) and relevant certifications will be considered for senior roles.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Responsibilities**\n* Derive, develop, and quantify data fusion algorithms and techniques to enhance sensor data integration and analysis.\n* Author, review, and maintain detailed technical documentation, including requirements, algorithm analysis memos, and design descriptions.\n* Analyze the accuracy, reliability, and effectiveness of data fusion techniques through rigorous testing and validation.\n* Develop and prototype algorithms using programming languages such as C\\+\\+, Python, and MATLAB, ensuring robustness and efficiency.\n* Collaborate with software architects and engineering teams to inform effective algorithm implementation and system design.\n* Collect, organize, and analyze large datasets from multiple sensors, synthesizing findings to support decision\\-making and system improvements.\n* Partner with customers and stakeholders to develop clear requirements and ensure solutions meet operational needs.\n* Participate in continuous process improvement initiatives to optimize software development workflows and technical outcomes.\n\n\n**Benefits**\n Boeing offers a comprehensive Total Rewards package designed to attract, engage, and retain top talent. Employees are eligible for competitive base pay, variable incentives, and a variety of benefit programs. These benefits typically include health insurance options, flexible spending accounts, health savings accounts, retirement savings plans, life and disability insurance, and paid time off. The company emphasizes work\\-life balance and provides programs for personal development, wellness, and financial security.\n   \n\n  \n\n Specific benefits may vary based on geographic location, employment status, and other factors. Employees also have access to professional development opportunities, tuition reimbursement, and employee assistance programs. The company’s commitment to diversity and inclusion ensures a supportive environment where all employees can thrive and advance their careers.\n   \n\n  \n\n Equal Opportunity\n   \n\n  \n\n Boeing is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace where employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, physical or mental disability, genetic factors, military/veteran status, or other characteristics protected by law. We believe that a diverse workforce fosters innovation and reflects the communities we serve. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will be considered for employment based on their skills, experience, and qualifications.","https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4428099266":"Role: Graph Data Scientist\n \n\n\n\n Location: Charlotte, NC(Onsite)\n \n\n\n\n Job Type: Long Term Contract\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n Job Description:\n \n\n\n\n Graph Data Scientist (Neo4j / TigerGraph \\+ Data Science)\n \n\n\n\n We are looking for a highly skilled Graph Data Scientist to design and develop graph\\-based analytical solutions leveraging Neo4j/TigerGraph and advanced data science techniques. The role will focus on building knowledge graphs, detecting complex patterns, and enabling AI\\-driven insights.\n \n\n\n\n Key Responsibilities\n \n\n\n\n • Design and develop graph data models using Neo4j/TigerGraph\n \n\n\n\n • Build and manage knowledge graphs for enterprise use cases (fraud detection, relationship mapping, pattern discovery)\n \n\n\n\n • Apply data science and ML techniques to extract insights from graph data\n \n\n\n\n • Develop graph algorithms (pathfinding, centrality, clustering, anomaly detection)\n \n\n\n\n • Integrate graph platforms with Gen AI/LLM\\-based systems for intelligent decision\\-making\n \n\n\n\n • Collaborate with engineering and AI teams to embed graph insights into application\n \n\n\n\n Required Skill\n \n\n\n\n • Strong experience in Neo4j, TigerGraph, or similar graph databases\n \n\n\n\n • Solid background in data science (Python, Pandas, Scikit\\-learn, PyTorch/TensorFlow)\n \n\n\n\n • Experience in graph algorithms and network analysis\n \n\n\n\n • Hands\\-on with data modeling, ETL, and large\\-scale data processing\n \n\n\n\n • Understanding of Gen AI / LLM integration with structured data systems\n \n\n\n\n Preferred\n \n\n\n\n • Experience with knowledge graphs and semantic data models\n \n\n\n\n • Exposure to hybrid architectures combining graph \\+ AI systems\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Thanks \\& Regards\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Himanshu Verma \\| Recruiter – US Staffing\n \n\n\n\n Email: Himanshu.v@ampstek.com \\| Desk: (609\\)\\-527\\-8914\n \n\n\n\n Ampstek LLC – Global IT Partner \\| www.ampstek.com","https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4428098464":"**About The Company**\n JPMorgan Chase \\& Co. is a leading global financial services firm with a rich history spanning over 200 years. Renowned for its innovative approach and commitment to excellence, the company offers a wide range of financial services including investment banking, asset management, retail banking, and treasury services. With a strong presence in over 100 countries, JPMorgan Chase \\& Co. is dedicated to providing exceptional solutions to its clients and fostering sustainable growth through responsible banking practices. The company's culture emphasizes integrity, diversity, and inclusion, making it an employer of choice for talented professionals worldwide.\n   \n\n  \n\n**About The Role**\n The role at JPMorgan Chase \\& Co. involves contributing to the development and execution of strategic initiatives within the financial services division. This position requires a detail\\-oriented and proactive professional who can analyze complex data, support project management activities, and collaborate with cross\\-functional teams to achieve organizational goals. The successful candidate will play a vital role in enhancing operational efficiency, implementing innovative solutions, and ensuring compliance with industry regulations. This role offers an excellent opportunity for individuals seeking to grow their career within a dynamic and globally recognized financial institution.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Qualifications**\n The ideal candidate should possess a bachelor’s degree in finance, economics, business administration, or a related field. A minimum of 3\\-5 years of experience in financial services, project management, or a similar role is preferred. Strong analytical skills, proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite, and familiarity with financial modeling and data analysis tools are essential. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills are required to effectively collaborate with diverse teams and stakeholders. A demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities, work under pressure, and adapt to changing environments is also important. Professional certifications such as CFA, CPA, or PMP are advantageous but not mandatory.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Responsibilities**\n In this role, you will be responsible for supporting the planning, execution, and monitoring of key projects within the organization. Your tasks will include conducting detailed financial analysis, preparing reports and presentations for senior management, and ensuring project deliverables are met on time and within budget. You will collaborate with various departments to gather requirements, identify risks, and develop mitigation strategies. Additionally, you will assist in maintaining compliance with regulatory standards and internal policies. Your role will also involve continuous process improvement initiatives, leveraging technology to streamline operations, and contributing to a culture of innovation and excellence.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Benefits**\n JPMorgan Chase \\& Co. offers a comprehensive benefits package designed to support the well\\-being and professional growth of its employees. This includes competitive salary packages, health insurance plans, retirement savings options, and paid time off. The company provides opportunities for continuous learning through training programs, workshops, and tuition reimbursement. Employees also enjoy a flexible work environment, wellness programs, and various employee resource groups that promote diversity and inclusion. JPMorgan Chase \\& Co. is committed to fostering a supportive workplace where employees can thrive and achieve their career aspirations.\n   \n\n  \n\n Equal Opportunity\n   \n\n  \n\n JPMorgan Chase \\& Co. is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We do not discriminate based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, age, disability, or any other legally protected status. We believe that a diverse workforce fosters innovation and drives better business outcomes. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to any protected characteristic.","https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4428091309":"Role: Graph Data Scientist(Neo4j / TigerGraph \\+ Data Science)\n \n\n\n\n Location: Charlotte, NC (Onsite)\n \n\n\n\n Job Type: Long Term Contract\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Job Description:\n \n\n\n\n We are looking for a highly skilled Graph Data Scientist to design and develop graph\\-based analytical solutions leveraging Neo4j/TigerGraph and advanced data science techniques. The role will focus on building knowledge graphs, detecting complex patterns, and enabling AI\\-driven insights.\n \n\n\n\n Key Responsibilities\n \n\n\n\n • Design and develop graph data models using Neo4j/TigerGraph\n \n\n\n\n • Build and manage knowledge graphs for enterprise use cases (fraud detection, relationship mapping, pattern discovery)\n \n\n\n\n • Apply data science and ML techniques to extract insights from graph data\n \n\n\n\n • Develop graph algorithms (pathfinding, centrality, clustering, anomaly detection)\n \n\n\n\n • Integrate graph platforms with Gen AI/LLM\\-based systems for intelligent decision\\-making\n \n\n\n\n • Collaborate with engineering and AI teams to embed graph insights into applications\n \n\n\n\n Required Skills\n \n\n\n\n • Strong experience in\n **Neo4j, TigerGraph, or similar graph databases** \n\n\n\n\n • Solid background in data science (Python, Pandas, Scikit\\-learn, PyTorch/TensorFlow)\n \n\n\n\n • Experience in graph algorithms and network analysis\n \n\n\n\n • Hands\\-on with data modeling, ETL, and large\\-scale data processing\n \n\n\n\n • Understanding of Gen AI / LLM integration with structured data systems\n \n\n\n\n Preferred\n \n\n\n\n • Experience with knowledge graphs and semantic data models\n \n\n\n\n • Exposure to hybrid architectures combining graph \\+ AI systems\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Thanks and regards,\n \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n Deepa Maurya \\| Technical Recruiter \\- US Staffing\n \n\n\n\n Email: deepa.m@ampstek.com \\| Desk: (609\\) 527\\-8971\n \n\n\n\n Ampstek LLC – Global IT Partner \\| www.ampstek.com","https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4428090850":"**About The Company**\n Boeing is a leading global aerospace company renowned for its innovation, technological excellence, and commitment to making the world a better place. With a rich history spanning over a century, Boeing designs, manufactures, and services commercial airplanes, defense, space, and security systems. The company prides itself on fostering a diverse and inclusive environment that encourages professional growth and development. Through cutting\\-edge research and development initiatives, Boeing continuously pushes the boundaries of aerospace technology, contributing to safer, more efficient, and sustainable transportation and defense solutions worldwide.\n   \n\n  \n\n**About The Role**\n We are seeking a highly skilled Software Engineer specializing in development for our Phantom Works Advanced Mission Planning team based in Berkeley, MO. This role is integral to supporting Boeing Defense, Space \\& Security's Software Engineering organization. The successful candidate will be responsible for designing, developing, testing, and maintaining sophisticated software solutions for autonomous systems, contributing to innovative projects that extend current capabilities and explore new markets. The position requires a collaborative mindset, a passion for solving complex problems, and an eagerness to work with emerging technologies in a fast\\-paced environment.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Qualifications**\n The ideal candidate will possess a bachelor's degree in engineering, computer science, or a related field, or have equivalent professional experience. Candidates must have the ability to obtain a U.S. Secret Security Clearance post\\-start. A minimum of five years of relevant software engineering experience, with proficiency in C\\+\\+, is required. Experience with autonomy, robotics software techniques, real\\-time software development, and Agile methodologies is essential. For senior roles, candidates with over nine years of experience, including familiarity with mission system architectures and electromagnetic warfare, are preferred. An active security clearance and familiarity with software development tools such as JIRA, GIT, and Jenkins are highly desirable.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Responsibilities**\n* Design, develop, test, and maintain non\\-embedded software throughout its lifecycle, ensuring compliance with industry standards, safety regulations, and customer requirements.\n* Analyze customer requirements and translate them into effective software designs and specifications.\n* Lead and mentor junior engineers, fostering a collaborative and productive team environment.\n* Develop use cases and perform software architecture trade studies to meet evolving project needs.\n* Define interfaces and perform unit and integration testing to ensure software quality and reliability.\n* Participate in peer reviews, system, and flight testing activities, and create comprehensive software documentation.\n* Support the integration of software solutions into larger systems, troubleshooting issues as they arise.\n* Engage in continuous process improvement initiatives, adopting best practices and new technologies to enhance development efficiency.\n\n\n**Benefits**\n At Boeing, we are committed to providing a comprehensive Total Rewards package designed to attract, engage, and retain top talent. Our benefits include competitive base salary, performance\\-based incentives, and a range of health and wellness programs. Eligible employees can enroll in health insurance plans, flexible spending accounts, health savings accounts, retirement savings plans, and life and disability insurance. We also support work\\-life balance through paid time off, parental leave, and other leave programs. Additionally, Boeing offers professional development opportunities, tuition reimbursement, and a collaborative work environment that encourages innovation and growth. The pay range for this role varies based on experience, with experienced candidates earning between $126,650 and $171,350, and senior candidates earning between $160,650 and $217,350\\. Potential signing bonuses are available for qualified external candidates.\n   \n\n  \n\n Equal Opportunity\n   \n\n  \n\n Boeing is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We are committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace where employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, age, disability, genetic factors, military/veteran status, or other protected characteristics. We believe in fostering an environment that respects and values individual differences, ensuring equal access to opportunities for all employees and applicants."}
